        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-30T05:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would like to ask why we have added the system libs only when !ctx.static(). I think that is the real problem.\n\nThis already makes foo.c below to be compiled differently (even without this CL)\n\n1) cc_library_shared { name: \"libfoo\", src: [\"foo.c\"] } // not cc_library but cc_library_shared\n2) cc_library_shared { name: \"libfoo\", whole_static_libs: [\"libfoo_static\"] }\n   cc_library_static { name: \"libfoo_static\", srcs: [\"foo.c\"] }\n\nThe former is with \n-Iexternal/libcxx/include \n-Iexternal/libcxxabi/include \n-Ibionic/libc/include \n-Ibionic/libc/system_properties/include \n-Isystem/core/property_service/libpropertyinfoparser/include \n\nwhile the latter is with\n-Iexternal/libcxx/include \n-Iexternal/libcxxabi/include \n\nIf you agree that this is a problem to be solved, I would like to handle it later in a separate CL.\n\nAnd as you said, since this pattern is not popular in Soong, I don\u0027t see an immediate breakage due to this.",
      "parentUuid": "165158f2_9b58d51d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 47,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 27
      },
